# LABEL_JOB_ABOUT_ROLE=About the job
# LABEL_JOB_ROLE_DUTIES=What you'd do
# LABEL_JOB_ROLE_ASKS=What they ask for
# LABEL_JOB_ROLE_NICE=Nice to have
# LABEL_JOB_ROLE_ALSO=Also mentioned
# MSG_JOB_NO_SUMMARY=TailorIT has no summary of this posting yet.
# LABEL_JOB_ABOUT_COMPANY=About {company}
# MSG_JOB_SUMMARY_FAILED=No summary: here is the posting as written.
# end v31 FIX-JOBS
# v33 JOBDETAIL: the job's details at once (the header's live line, Requirements at a glance, Skills, Benefits, the
# Summary | Full posting switch).
# LABEL_JOB_CHECKED_LIVE=Checked live {when}
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE=Requirements at a glance
# MSG_JOB_GLANCE_TIP=What the posting asks for, checked against your profile.
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_EXPERIENCE=Experience
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_EDUCATION=Education
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_CERTIFICATIONS=Licences & certifications
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_NOT_STATED=Not stated
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_EQUIVALENT=or equivalent experience
# LABEL_JOB_GLANCE_HAVE_IT=You have it
# MSG_JOB_GLANCE_MEETS=Your profile meets this.
# MSG_JOB_GLANCE_BELOW=This asks for more than your profile shows.
# MSG_JOB_GLANCE_UNKNOWN=Add this to your Autofill profile to check it.
# LABEL_JOB_SKILLS=Skills
# MSG_JOB_SKILLS_HIGHLIGHT=Skills from your resume are highlighted
# LABEL_JOB_BENEFITS=Benefits
# LABEL_JOB_SUMMARY=Summary
# LABEL_JOB_FULL_POSTING=Full posting
# LABEL_JOB_DETAIL_TAILOR=Tailor my resume
# end v33 JOBDETAIL
# v32 ADMINAPP: an admin publishes a job TailorIT couldn't read as it was captured (Admin › Review), at most this many an hour.
# ADMIN_APPROVALS_PER_HOUR=300
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_APPROVED_BODY=An admin checked the posting TailorIT couldn't read and published it as you added it.
# end v32 ADMINAPP
# v32 JOBS2
# MSG_JOB_MATCH_TIP=How many of the posting's keywords your resume has.
# end v32 JOBS2
# v33 ROLES: the person's field (a resume's Field, Settings › Account's Your field, the Jobs page's My field).
# LABEL_RESUME_FIELD=Field
# MSG_RESUME_FIELD_TIP=The kind of work this resume is for: TailorIT tailors it and writes for it in that field.
# LABEL_RESUME_FIELD_DETECT=Detect automatically
# MSG_RESUME_FIELD_DETECTED=Detected: {field}
# MSG_RESUME_FIELD_SAVE_FAILED=Your field wasn't saved. Choose it again to retry.
# LABEL_ACCOUNT_YOUR_FIELD=Your field
# MSG_ACCOUNT_YOUR_FIELD={field} (from your default resume)
# MSG_ACCOUNT_FIELD_NONE=Add a resume and TailorIT works out your field from it.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_FIELD_TIP=Change it on your default resume's Field; tailoring and the Jobs page's My field follow it.
# LABEL_JOBS_MY_FIELD=My field
# MSG_JOBS_MY_FIELD_TIP=Jobs in your field, {field}, from your default resume.
# end v33 ROLES
# v32 INT-1: the mark of a job an admin published as it was captured, and its "?".
# LABEL_JOB_APPROVED_BY_ADMIN=Approved by an admin
# MSG_JOB_APPROVED_BY_ADMIN=TailorIT couldn't read this posting, so an admin checked it.
# end v32 INT-1
# v32 FIX-API: an admin's approval keeps its job in search this many days; the approval notices; Fill from my resume's marks.
# ADMIN_APPROVED_JOB_DAYS=30
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_APPROVED_TITLE=Approved by an admin: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_PUBLIC_VERSION_TITLE=Published for everyone: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_PUBLIC_VERSION_BODY=An admin published another version of this job for everyone; yours stays as you added it.
# LABEL_AUTOFILL_AI_READ=AI read, check it
# MSG_AUTOFILL_SEED_AI_CHECK=The AI read your file: check each field marked "AI read" before you save.
# MSG_AUTOFILL_SEED_NO_RESUME_IN_FILE=The AI found no resume in it.
# LABEL_AUTOFILL_CHECK_THESE=Check these
# MSG_AUTOFILL_CHECK_THESE_TIP=Fill could not be sure of these, so check them before you save.
# MSG_AUTOFILL_FILL_NO_RESUME=Add a resume to fill from it.
# LABEL_AUTOFILL_ADD_RESUME=Add a resume
# end v32 FIX-API
# v34 PUBLIC: reads of the public constants one network address may make a minute while signed out (the public pages).
# OPERATOR_NAME and OPERATOR_WEBSITE are under Sign-in, above.
# PUBLIC_PAGE_READS_PER_MINUTE=120
# end v34 PUBLIC
# v34 MCPDIR: one MCP tool answer's size and one call's time (Claude's directory: about 150,000 characters, 240 s).
# MCP_RESULT_MAX_CHARS=75000
# MCP_TOOL_TIME_LIMIT_MS=200000
# MSG_MCP_TOOL_TOO_SLOW={tool} did not finish within {seconds} seconds, so TailorIT stopped waiting. {check}
# end v34 MCPDIR
# v34 FANOUT: one action on several profiles (Save to, Copy to, the All profiles bulk, filters for every profile): the
# refusals.
# MSG_FANOUT_TOO_MANY_PROFILES=Choose at most {max} profiles at once.
# MSG_FANOUT_TOO_MANY_JOBS=Choose at most {max} jobs at once.
# MSG_FANOUT_FILTER_TEXT=Write the custom filter in plain words, without tags or markers, then save again.
# MSG_FANOUT_PROFILE_FAILED=Something failed on our side for this profile. Try it again.
# MSG_FANOUT_PROFILE_UNUSABLE=This profile isn't available for this action.
# end v34 FANOUT
# v34 ACCTDEL: deleting an account (Settings › Account › Delete my account; Admin › Users › Delete account).
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_EMAIL=Type the email address of the account exactly as it is shown, then delete it.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_LAST_ADMIN=This is the only administrator account that can sign in. Make another account an administrator first, then delete this one.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_OWN=You cannot delete the account you are signed in with here. Use Settings › Account › Delete my account.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_BLOCKED=This account cannot be deleted right now because of a problem on our side. Ask an administrator of this installation to look at the server's log.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETED=We deleted your account and everything in it.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_PENDING=We turned your account off and are deleting it. That finishes on its own within a day; there is nothing more to do.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_DELETE_PENDING_ADMIN=The account is off and being deleted. That finishes on its own within a day, or delete it again to finish it now.
# MSG_ACCOUNT_BEING_DELETED=This account is being deleted. That finishes within a day; then this address can start a new account.
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARED_PROFILE_DELETED_TITLE=A profile shared with you was deleted
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARED_PROFILE_DELETED_BODY=Its owner deleted their account, so it is no longer among your profiles. Settings › Sharing shows what is shared now.
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARED_PROFILE_DELETED_ADMIN_BODY=The account that shared it with you was deleted, so it is no longer among your profiles. Settings › Sharing shows what is shared now.
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARE_GRANTEE_DELETED_TITLE=A share of your profile ended
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARE_GRANTEE_DELETED_BODY=Someone you shared your profile with deleted their account, so they no longer see it. Settings › Sharing shows what is shared now.
# MSG_NOTIFY_SHARE_GRANTEE_DELETED_ADMIN_BODY=An account you shared your profile with was deleted, so it no longer sees it. Settings › Sharing shows what is shared now.
# end v34 ACCTDEL
# v34 DIRKIT: whether report_unsupported keeps the words of the person's request. Turn it off on a server listed in
# Claude's Connectors Directory (docs/directory/CHECKLIST.md): only what TailorIT lacks and the tools tried are kept.
# MCP_REPORT_REQUEST_TEXT=true
# end v34 DIRKIT
# v35 IMPORT: imports of job links (Admin › Import; Jobs › Add job › File, Google Sheet): a person's rows per
# import and per day (counted toward the person acting), the request rate, and the words.
# JOB_IMPORT_ROWS_MAX=200
# FREE_JOB_IMPORT_ROWS_PER_DAY=100
# PAID_JOB_IMPORT_ROWS_PER_DAY=1000
# JOB_IMPORTS_PER_MINUTE=20
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_TOO_MANY_ROWS=Import at most {max} rows at a time; this one has {rows}. Split it and import each part.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_DAY_LIMIT=You imported {limit} rows in the last 24 hours: try again in {hours} {hours|hour|hours}.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_OVER_DAY=Over today's rows: import it again in {hours} {hours|hour|hours}.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_NO_LINK_COLUMN=Choose the column that holds the job links.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_EMPTY=There are no rows to import: check the file or the tab.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_BUSY=You sent many imports at once: try again in a minute.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_FILE_UNREADABLE=TailorIT cannot read this file: save it as .xlsx, .csv, .tsv, .txt or .json and try again.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_FILE_TOO_BIG=This spreadsheet is too large once opened: save fewer rows or columns and try again.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_NO_LINK=This row has no job link.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_REPEATS=Repeats row {row}.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_HOST=Can't import from {host}.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_WAITING=Already waiting for review.
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_TITLE=Your import of {rows} {rows|row|rows} finished
# end v35 IMPORT
# v35 ADMIN: how long one request of a Review lane's "Select all" decision runs before it answers (v3.6.1: every lane).
# ADMIN_BULK_ALL_SECONDS=20
# end v35 ADMIN
# v36 IMPORTTIME: a job an admin imports shows the import time; it reads "Reposted" when its board posted it more
# than this many days before the import, else "Posted".
# ADMIN_IMPORT_REPOSTED_AFTER_DAYS=7
# end v36 IMPORTTIME
# v35 FIX-STORE: a person's reads of their imports a minute, the largest "Download these rows" file, and the words of a
# Google Sheet linked to another account (a sheet belongs to the first account that reads it).
# JOB_IMPORT_READS_PER_MINUTE=120
# JOB_IMPORT_DOWNLOAD_MAX_MB=10
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_SHEET_CLAIMED=This sheet is linked to another TailorIT account. Make a copy of it, share the copy with TailorIT's address (Viewer), and import the copy.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_SHEET_TAB_NOT_FOUND=This tab can't be found: choose a tab from the list.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_READS_BUSY=You opened import results many times in a minute: wait a minute and open them again.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_DOWNLOAD_TOO_BIG=These rows make a file over {max} MB. Fill in Company and Title in your own file or sheet and import it again.
# The "import finished" notice, a part per count above 0 (joined: "8 jobs waiting for review, 4 need a title and company.").
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_ADDED={added} added
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_KNOWN={known} already in TailorIT
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_REVIEW={review} {review|job|jobs} waiting for review
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_NEEDS_DETAILS={needs_details} {needs_details|needs|need} a title and company
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_CLOSED={closed} closed
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_IMPORT_PART_FAILED={failed} not imported
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_ADDED_HELD=Added; waiting for approval in New jobs
# end v35 FIX-STORE
# v35 IMPORTWEB: the limits line under an import (Admin › Import; Jobs › Add job › File, Google Sheet).
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROWS_UP_TO=Up to {max} rows a file or sheet.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROWS_LEFT_TODAY=You can import {rows} more {rows|row|rows} today.
# MSG_ADMIN_IMPORT_PASTE_UP_TO=Up to {max} pasted links or rows; a file or a Google Sheet takes up to {file_max} rows.
# end v35 IMPORTWEB
# v35 FIX-WEB: Add job's words when only some of a file's rows fit today, and when none is left (the final review's M1).
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_OVER_TODAY=Only the first {fit} {fit|row fits|rows fit} today; the other {over} won't be imported. Import the file again in 24 hours for the rest: rows already added are skipped.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_NONE_LEFT_TODAY=You have no rows left to import today: import again in 24 hours.
# end v35 FIX-WEB
# v36 SOURCES: Run now and a run's Continue on a job source that is off (only an admin turns a source on).
# MSG_INGEST_SOURCE_OFF=It is off: turn it on first.
# end v36 SOURCES
# v36 APPLYAPI: Share All (Auto-apply) shares at most this many saved jobs a press, the newest first, and its refusal past it.
# SHARE_ALL_MAX=500
# MSG_SHARE_ALL_TOO_MANY=Share at most {max} saved jobs at once.
# end v36 APPLYAPI
# v37 LANE: every Workday site shares one lane: one request at a time this gap apart; discovery checks at most this
# many Workday boards an hour. Every lane (Workday's in v3.6.1) adapts to 429s: a 429 pauses the lane (30 s, doubled at
# each 429 in the window, up to the cap) and widens its gap (doubled per 429, up to the widest, halving back after each
# calm stretch); enough 429s in the window hold the lane; Run now's answer while another source of the lane runs.
# WORKDAY_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=3000
# WORKDAY_DISCOVERY_PER_HOUR=120
# LANE_429_WINDOW_MINUTES=60
# LANE_PAUSE_MAX_MINUTES=30
# LANE_MAX_INTERVAL_MS=30000
# LANE_EASE_MINUTES=10
# LANE_BREAKER_HOLD_MINUTES=60
# MSG_INGEST_LANE_RUNNING=Another {site} source is running. Try again when it ends.
# end v37 LANE
# v37 CLOSED: how long the link queue reads again a link whose site failed for now (or paused TailorIT) before an
# import's row goes to Review, and how long one queued read may take (its wait for the site's turn included).
# LINK_QUEUE_RETRY_HOURS=24
# LINK_QUEUE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# A person's read while a site (every Workday site) paused TailorIT; a closed report TailorIT's own read confirmed.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_PAUSED={site} asked us to slow down. Try again after {time}.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_HELD=TailorIT is waiting before it reads {site} again. Try again after {time}.
# MSG_REVIEW_CLOSED_CONFIRMED=Closed: confirmed by TailorIT
# end v37 CLOSED
# v37 FIX-REV: what waits in Admin › Review on a job a report, a purge or an admin closed is decided with these words;
# a person's Retry read that finds the posting closed.
# MSG_REVIEW_JOB_CLOSED=The job closed
# MSG_JOB_RETRY_CLOSED=This posting has closed, so TailorIT marked the job closed.
# An import's row waiting to be read again: while the site asked TailorIT to slow down, or after a failure for now.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_PAUSED={site} asked us to slow down; TailorIT reads the link again after {time}.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_LATER=TailorIT reads the link again after {time}.
# end v37 FIX-REV
# v37 BOARDS: BambooHR and iCIMS runs (per-posting reads of each run), and Run now on a source whose terms are not recorded.
# BAMBOOHR_READS_PER_RUN=100
# BAMBOOHR_RECHECK_DAYS=7
# ICIMS_READS_PER_RUN=100
# ICIMS_RECHECK_DAYS=7
# ICIMS_UNLISTED_RECHECK_HOURS=24
# MSG_INGEST_SOURCE_TERMS=Its terms are {status}: TailorIT doesn't read it.
# end v37 BOARDS
# v37 TRANSFER: Admin › Sources' sources file (Import, Export): the most sources it holds, and the refusals.
# ADMIN_SOURCES_IMPORT_MAX=5000
# MSG_ADMIN_SOURCES_FILE_TOO_MANY=This file holds {count} sources; a file may hold at most {max}. Split it and import each part.
# MSG_ADMIN_SOURCES_EXPORT_TOO_MANY={count} sources match; a file holds at most {max}. Narrow the filters (a kind, a search) and export each part.
# MSG_ADMIN_SOURCES_FILE_INVALID=This isn't a TailorIT sources file. Choose a file saved by Export in Admin › Sources.
# MSG_ADMIN_SOURCES_FILE_UP_TO=Up to {max} sources a file.
# end v37 TRANSFER
# v37 FIX-37B: a board whose source's terms don't allow reading is never read: a person's link to it, an import's row.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_TERMS=TailorIT doesn't read this company's job site. Add the title and company to save it for yourself.
# MSG_JOB_IMPORT_ROW_TERMS=TailorIT doesn't read {host}: its terms say no.
# end v37 FIX-37B
# v37 INT-2b: BambooHR and iCIMS each share one lane, as Workday does: one request at a time to all of the platform,
# this gap apart; discovery checks at most this many of each platform's boards an hour (0 stops those checks).
# BAMBOOHR_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=2000
# BAMBOOHR_DISCOVERY_PER_HOUR=120
# ICIMS_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=2000
# ICIMS_DISCOVERY_PER_HOUR=120
# end v37 INT-2b

